+/// pokezero gen3 fidelity fix: is this turn a CONTINUATION of a lock, i.e. one
+/// on which Showdown's `getLockedMove()` returns a move and the PP deduction is
+/// skipped entirely?
+///
+/// Two sources, because the engine represents them differently.
+/// `charge_continuation` is passed in for the second half of a two-turn move:
+/// the charge volatile is cleared earlier in `generate_instructions_from_move`,
+/// before the deduction runs, so the fact has to be carried in a local rather
+/// than re-read here. The LOCKEDMOVE volatile is still live at deduction time
+/// for Outrage-class locks, so it can be read directly.
+///
+/// Deliberately NOT included: MUSTRECHARGE. Showdown's `mustrecharge` is a
+/// `LockMove` provider too, but the engine already models a recharge turn as
+/// `MoveChoice::None`, and `Choices::NONE` returns from
+/// `generate_instructions_from_move` long before any deduction — so a recharge
+/// turn is already free and adding it here would be dead weight.
+fn in_locked_turn(
+    state: &State,
+    side_ref: &SideReference,
+    charge_continuation: bool,
+) -> bool {
+    charge_continuation
+        || state
+            .get_side_immutable(side_ref)
+            .volatile_statuses
+            .contains(&PokemonVolatileStatus::LOCKEDMOVE)
 }
 
